Never weaken, delete, skip, or relax a test to make an implementation pass.
Always write adversarial tests before implementation.
Never hand-write research signals; signals must be generated through the grammar.
Do not add an agent framework or machine learning.
Never use a negative shift, a centered rolling window, or a negative lag.
Never fill, forward-fill, backward-fill, or otherwise impute NaN price data.
Never use `if paper` outside `cq/execution/`.
Never implement live execution; it must remain an explicit NotImplementedError.
Apply execution lag in exactly one location.
Always report both gross and net performance.
Always report the exact test count.
